# The engine validates every request, and the command line explains what it can't parse. Nothing changes either way.
> buy 10 @ 100.00
error: there are no symbols yet: try add ACME
> add ACME
added ACME

# Rejected by the engine.
> buy 0 @ 100.00
ACME #1 BUY 0 @ 100.00 -> rejected: INVALID_QUANTITY
> buy 10 @ 0
ACME #2 BUY 10 @ 0.00 -> rejected: INVALID_PRICE
> sell 10 @ 100.00 display=20
ACME #3 SELL 10 @ 100.00 display 20 -> rejected: INVALID_DISPLAY_QUANTITY
> buy 10 market post-only
ACME #4 BUY 10 @ market post-only -> rejected: INVALID_POST_ONLY
> cancel 42
ACME #42 cancel rejected: UNKNOWN_ORDER
> buy 10 @ 100.00 id=5
ACME #5 BUY 10 @ 100.00 -> resting 10
> buy 10 @ 100.00 id=5
ACME #5 BUY 10 @ 100.00 -> rejected: DUPLICATE_ORDER_ID

# Rejected by the command line.
> buy 10 @ 100.001
error: expected a price such as 100.25, got '100.001'
> stop buy 10
error: stop orders need '@ STOP_PRICE'
> frobnicate
error: unknown command 'frobnicate' (try help)
> buy 10 @ 100.00 color=red
error: unknown option 'color'
> book GLOBEX
error: unknown symbol GLOBEX (add it first)
> book
ACME  CONTINUOUS  last -  resting 1
              BID                       ASK
     100.00 x 10      (1)
